    "body": "### What does this PR do?\n\nFixes the rendering of the \"Formal derivation\" in §3.2.2 *Policy Gradient Loss (with IS/RS Correction)* of [`docs/algo/rollout_corr_math.md`](https://verl.readthedocs.io/en/latest/algo/rollout_corr_math.html#policy-gradient-loss-with-is-rs-correction).\n\nIn steps 2–4, each `$$ … $$` block starts on the line right after the list item's text, with no blank line in between. MyST therefore parses it as inline double-dollar math within the paragraph, and the rendered page shows stray `$` signs around the equations (for example `$\\( J(\\theta) = … \\)$`). This PR adds a blank line before each of the three blocks so they render as display math.\n\n### Checklist Before Starting\n\n- [x] Search for similar PRs. Paste at least one query link here: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=rollout_corr_math (no matches)\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}` (This will be checked by the CI)\n\n### Test\n\nDocs-only change. I parsed the section with `markdown-it-py` + `mdit_py_plugins.dollarmath` (the parser MyST uses):\n- before: the three equations are tokens of type `math_inline_double` (inline, which shows the stray `$` signs)\n- after: the three equations are tokens of type `math_block` (display)\n\n### API and Usage Example\n\nN/A\n\n### Design & Code Changes\n\n- `docs/algo/rollout_corr_math.md`: add a blank line before the `$$` display blocks in steps 2, 3 and 4 of the formal derivation in §3.2.2.\n\n### Checklist Before Submitting\n\n- [x] Read the [Contribute Guide](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [ ] Apply [pre-commit checks](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-linting-and-formatting): `pre-commit install && pre-commit run --all-files --show-diff-on-failure --color=always`\n- [x] Add / Update [the documentation](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/tree/main/docs).\n- [ ] Add unit or end-to-end test(s) to [the CI workflow](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/tree/main/.github/workflows) to cover all the code. If not feasible, explain why: docs-only whitespace fix, no code changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
